  "amount_units": "dollars",

  "_readme": [
    "The spend report a Claude Team or Enterprise plan exports from",
    "Settings > Analytics > 'Export spend report'. This is not the Developer",
    "Console's Usage or Cost export: it covers seat-plan usage (chat, Claude",
    "Code, Cowork), one row per person per model, summed across the date range",
    "chosen when exporting. There is no date column and no time breakdown.",
    "",
    "Source: Anthropic support article 12883420, 'View usage analytics for Team",
    "and Enterprise plans', read 2026-10-03. It names these columns verbatim:",
    "",
    "  total_requests, total_prompt_tokens, total_completion_tokens,",
    "  total_net_spend_usd, total_gross_spend_usd",
    "",
    "and describes the rest only in prose: the user's email, account UUID,",
    "product, and model and model family. A third-party write-up also mentions",
    "total_cache_read_tokens and total_web_search_count. No genuine export has",
    "been seen, so every alias below the verbatim names is a guess. That is why",
    "each field carries many of them, and why this profile is provisional.",
    "",
    "The usual rules still hold. A missing required column fails with the real",
    "header row printed. Two columns claiming one field is an error, never a",
    "coin flip. An unrecognised column is reported, never silently dropped.",
    "Run with --explain-schema to see the mapping that was applied.",
    "",
    "Spend columns are read as dollars: their documented names end in _usd.",
    "Generic spellings ('spend', 'cost', 'amount') map to net spend, since net",
    "is what is actually paid. A file carrying both a generic column and a net",
    "one stops with an ambiguity error rather than picking one.",
    "",
    "When you have a real export: correct the aliases, set 'status' to",
    "'verified', and record the export date in 'verified_against'. No code",
    "change is needed."
  ],

